      "created_at": "2013-08-27T15:54:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ameena\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/48/1907_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ameena:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We play with three heroes (though there's only two of us) and we don't generally find Miss Information too hard - I suppose it's because you need less Clue cards out before she flips. One time we fought her, I played Omni-10 and I felt as though I'd practically soloed her with all my components and stuff :D.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I think that's the clarifier.&nbsp; If you have deck manipulation via The Wraith, Visionary, Omnitron-X, etc. in a three hero game then she can be a cakewalk.&nbsp; If you don't, then you have a huge potential of playing a very long, very painful, very dull waiting game.</p>",
